WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.901
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:05.133
you know from shows
like "Big Little Lies,"

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.567
"Parks and Recreation"
and "Severance."

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:09.334
He stars in the long-awaited
third season of "Party Down."

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.234
The season finale
premieres Friday on Starz.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:14.367
Let's take a look.
-Okay, everybody. Great job.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:16.400
-Yeah!
-Okay.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.300
There is kettle corn
and Sprite in the courtyard.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.434
-You guys got real Sprite?
-No, no.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.467
We've got...

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:24.968
store brand!

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:27.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes!

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.334
-Store brand! Yes!

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:32.167
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Adam Scott!

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:42.634
♪♪

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:50.400
♪♪

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.467
Welcome back to the show!
-Thank you so much.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.767
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.601
-We consider you family
here on the show.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:58.534
-Thank you very much.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:00:59.634
-We've known you
for a long time.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:02.133
And I was very happy
your actual family

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.300
was back in the green room.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.701
I got to say hello to them.
-Thank you.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.067
Yeah, they're here,
all three of them.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.300
I was about to say four,

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.534
but there's only three of them.
-Yeah.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.234
That would have
immediately made me think,

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.367
"Oh, you hired actors
to play your family."

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:16.067
-Yeah, and I can't
slip up like that.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.400
I can't let that happen.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.200
-And your kids are older
than mine.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.400
You've got a -- what?

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.033
I guess a 10th grader
and an 8th grader.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.334
-That's right. 16 and 14.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.234
-And the 16 year old, driving?

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:29.934
-Driving a car.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:32.968
-Yeah, he got his license
like a week and a half ago,

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:35.834
and it's terrifying.

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:40.000
But it's also kind of --
kind of great because now, like,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.400
I'm here working in New York.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.868
They live in Los Angeles,

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:48.234
so I have a GPS thing
so I can see him wherever he is.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:52.601
I can even see what miles per
hour he's going at all times.

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:55.567
-Now, does he know that
you can track him like that?

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.934
-He's finding out right now.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.934
-Yeah.
-Did you put a -- Did you, like,

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.067
put a tracker under the car?
-That's right.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.701
Just like in "Breaking Bad."
I put the thing...

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:06.100
under the thing.
-You're like,

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.367
"I'm just going to do
an oil check, son."

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.834
-That's right.
"Let me see here."

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.934
But he, like, calls me.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:15.868
He's like,
"I'm at 7-Eleven by myself."

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:20.133
And I'm like, "Yeah, I --
I know. I know exactly..."

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:23.300
Yeah. So it's scary,
but it's terrific for him.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.100
-Did you teach him
how to drive?

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.167
-I did.
I and my wife taught him...

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.734
-Yeah.
-...together.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:31.534
-I'm worried that my wife
thinks I'm such a bad driver

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.934
she's not going to let me teach
our kids how to drive.

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:35.100
-Right.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.834
-Like she's going
to handle the entire thing?

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.534
-Yeah. She's already said, "Me
and my father will handle it."

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:40.567
-[ Chuckles ] Wow.

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.667
-Which is massively
emasculating.

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.801
-So your father-in-law
will step in.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:45.834
-Yeah.
-That's terrible.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:47.434
-That is terrible.
-Yeah.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:50.300
-And then your --
What's your daughter into?

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.567
-She is primarily
right now into Taylor Swift.

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:54.701
-Okay.
-Right?

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:55.801
-I don't think
she's alone there.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:56.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's fine.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.200
Like, I am -- Like, great.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.801
That's a great thing.
-I will say of the music

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:03.033
a younger generation
can be into,

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:04.634
that is like so pleasant
and lovely.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:05.667
-100%.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.133
The thing that
she's into right now

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:09.601
is -- because her tour
is The Eras Tour.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.667
[ Applause ]
And so you --

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.667
Everything you say
about Taylor Swift

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.400
gets a round of applause
at all times.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.000
So you dress it --
When you go to that concert,

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.367
you dress up as whatever era
you're most into at the moment.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:27.167
And so she's going to dress up,
I think,

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.033
for the Reputation era.
-Oh, so

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.667
your daughter
has chosen her era.

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.501
-Chosen her era,
at least for now.

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:35.701
-Do you have a Taylor Swift era
that you prefer?

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:38.601
-Yeah. I mean, I feel like
I would -- I would probably go

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:41.267
in the, like, Evermore era.
-Right.

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:44.400
I will say, of men our age,
that's the costume...

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.467
-Probably.
Because that's just a cardigan.

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:48.400
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. That.
-And like a cup of tea.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.534
-[ Laughs ] Right. Yeah.

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:51.133
-Which is what
we're already doing.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.133
-Yeah. Yeah.
We're like -- People --

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.601
My kids will often walk in
when I'm drinking my tea

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:56.801
and they're like, "Is this
Eras?"

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:57.734
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yes!

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:58.901
-I'm in an era right now.

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:00.434
-I'm not just a dude
in a cardigan.

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:02.868
-No. That's not what I'm doing.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.167
-"Party Down."
This is so exciting

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:07.734
because this is a show --
you could attest to --

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:10.300
nobody was watching this show
when it was on.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:11.834
-No one.
-But then they found it

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:14.200
after the fact.
-Yeah, like seven years later.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.434
-What?

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:18.133
How few people were
watching it when you...?

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:23.701
-We got canceled, rightly so,
in 2010.

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:27.834
Our series finale
had 13,000 viewers...

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.834
[ Laughter ]
...so

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:32.133
we should have been canceled,
as it turns out.

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.534
-And that's a
TV show anyone could watch

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:37.033
that did like less numbers
than a Taylor Swift show.

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:39.234
-That's exactly right.
-Like a concert.

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:43.167
-Oh, one concert would dwarf
our entire audience.

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:44.667
-You could run out
on stage and be like,

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.400
"Before you guys go, do you mind
watching an episode

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.801
of 'Party Down'?"
-And like 8,000 would leave.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.300
-Was it a cool thing, though,
to find out...?

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.701
I mean, again,
it must have been disappointing

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.801
while you're making it
because it seemed like a show --

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:58.033
I have to believe
based on watching it --

00:04:58.033 --> 00:04:59.801
it seems like
it's a blast to make.

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:02.567
-Yeah, it was super fun
and everything.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:05.567
But, yeah, as we --
as the years went by,

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:07.367
people were kind of
catching on to it,

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:11.234
found its audience, and people
weren't even totally aware

00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:13.934
it was an older show,
that it got canceled

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:15.367
like eight years ago
or whatever.

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:18.067
So they would come up and say
how much they loved the show

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.968
and when's the next season
coming on?

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.000
And it's like, "No, that's over.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.300
Like, you can't --
It died.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.067
It's the late, great
'Party Down.'

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:29.934
It's dead."

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:31.801
-Very nicely done.
-Yeah.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:35.067
So, but now it is
actually back...

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:38.133
-And were you all just
collectively delighted

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:39.400
when this...?
-Yeah.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.734
-Yeah.
-Yeah. It was so fun.

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:44.100
I mean, it's almost like reboots
are like a cliche now.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.834
Everyone just says
how delighted

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:48.167
they are to be back
with all their friends, but

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:51.300
we were delighted to be
back with all of our friends.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.701
Because we really --
like, it ended

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:56.467
and we were so deeply bummed.

00:05:56.467 --> 00:06:01.167
But it also felt very
"Party Down" to be canceled.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:03.200
It kind of fit in
with the ethos of the show.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.767
-Right. Those characters...

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:07.100
If they were --
If those characters made a TV

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.534
show, it would definitely get
canceled.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:12.200
-Yes. If we won in any way,
it just wouldn't feel right.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.434
-I know you get approached
by fans all the time,

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:17.834
but I would imagine those
in the catering community

00:06:17.834 --> 00:06:19.567
feel a great connection
to this show.

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:21.634
-They do.
-And you must be at events

00:06:21.634 --> 00:06:23.667
where you interact
with caterers.

00:06:23.667 --> 00:06:27.467
-Yeah, they -- Yeah.
You find that the caterers

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:30.767
and the bartenders
are mostly "Party Down" fans

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:33.767
and feel like
an immediate kinship,

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:37.167
which is great because
I get like my sliders first.

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:40.334
-Oh, wow. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:42.100
It's funny because you don't
get them for free

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.934
because they're already free.
-They're already free.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:45.601
-But you get them first.
-And you don't want

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:48.667
them to zhuzh up your slider.
-Right, yeah.

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:51.567
-So just getting it
first ends up being the big win.

00:06:51.567 --> 00:06:52.901
-That's pretty -- I mean...
-Listen.

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:54.567
-You're living it pretty good
right now.

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:58.234
-Show business is pretty great.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:58.234 --> 00:07:00.834
You know, I'm very excited.
I know you're out here.

00:07:00.834 --> 00:07:02.367
You're filming the second season
of "Severance,"

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:04.801
a show we've talked about
that I just love.

00:07:04.801 --> 00:07:06.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:09.000
-Thanks.
-Tonally...

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.000
Tonally, it couldn't be more
different than "Party Down."

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.434
But there is a similarity, which
it's you have a [bleep] job.

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:16.567
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:18.601
-And I don't really like
doing it.

00:07:18.601 --> 00:07:20.567
-Yeah, but you try really hard.

00:07:20.567 --> 00:07:23.734
I mean, I think that's what --
you don't want

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:25.901
your colleagues to know
you think it's [bleep].

00:07:25.901 --> 00:07:27.133
-That's right.
-You're the guy who's, like,

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:29.300
holding out, trying to rally the
troops.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.567
-All of the effort
I put into the job

00:07:31.567 --> 00:07:35.767
is put into making it look
like I don't hate it

00:07:35.767 --> 00:07:39.033
or that I'm actually doing
something when I'm not.

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:41.701
That's where the two shows
share common ground.

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:43.868
-Well, it's nice that you have
that commonality.

00:07:43.868 --> 00:07:45.534
-That's right.
-Another show that you did

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:47.267
with a great cast was
"Parks and Rec."

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:48.400
-Yeah,
-And there was a guy --

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
There we go.

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:56.667
Our next guest, Jeff Tweedy,
did a cameo on "Parks and Rec,"

00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:59.734
and you look very happy to have
taken this photo with him.

00:07:59.734 --> 00:08:02.033
-I was so, so happy that day,

00:08:02.033 --> 00:08:05.267
that fine day
in 2000-whenever it was.

00:08:05.267 --> 00:08:08.200
It was fantastic.
2014, probably.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.200
-And he seems pretty psyched,
too.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.567
So that's -- Must have been
a nice moment.

00:08:11.567 --> 00:08:12.801
-I mean, it looks like he's --

00:08:12.801 --> 00:08:14.467
I remember when we met,
he was like,

00:08:14.467 --> 00:08:16.000
"Oh, my God, you're on the show.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.901
This is cool. It's weird
seeing you in person."

00:08:18.901 --> 00:08:20.934
And I was like,
"Are you [bleep] kidding me?

00:08:20.934 --> 00:08:22.434
Really?"

00:08:22.434 --> 00:08:24.968
And, yeah,
I was just delighted.

00:08:24.968 --> 00:08:28.167
-Well, it's also --
You know, being as big a fan

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:30.434
as I am of him
and his band and you,

00:08:30.434 --> 00:08:32.267
it's a very nice night
to have you all here together.

00:08:32.267 --> 00:08:34.701
So thank you for being here,
my friend.

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:36.767
You guys, that's Adam Scott.

00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:38.300
Third season finale of
"Party Down"

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.467
premieres Friday on Starz.

